# Bandit Level 1 → Level 2

## Level Goal
The password for the next level is stored in a file called `-` located in the home directory.

## Given Information
Username: bandit1  
Host: bandit.labs.overthewire.org  
Port: 2220  

## Approach
The file name begins with a dash, so it cannot be opened normally.

## Commands Used
ssh bandit1@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220  
ls  
cat ./-

## Explanation
When a file name starts with `-`, Linux thinks it is an option.  
Using `./-` tells the system it is a file in the current directory.

